### Rationale
H6 is refuted on the rented B200. None of the S-path variants (a–e) beat r0 by more than 2% at 7.9, 26 or 31 MB. The S time looks like the empty-kernel span plus one DRAM round trip plus streaming plus the harness's dirty-L2 write-backs, and none of those is something the kernel can change. I'm returning r0 with a 32-bit-address S path for rows ≤ 512. It ties r0 (S band +0.1%, M +0.0%, L +0.1%, all 16 workloads pass). It is the same code as variant (e) except that it keeps the evict_last stores.

